    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d472">

                <pb facs="0856" n="794" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg794"/>

                <head>No. 467.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-07-25"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 25, 1878</date>.
                        (Received August 17.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 102.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose for your
                    information a copy and translation of a circular issued yesterday by the
                    director-general of customs, <pb facs="0857" n="795" xml:id="pg795"/> in which,
                    are set forth such changes as have been made in the tariff by the bill of ways
                    and means of 1878–’79. One or two of these affect American interests. The
                    definition of what shall constitute a <hi rendition="#italic">direct</hi> voyage
                    from the Spanish West Indies to peninsular ports will, I trust, have the effect
                    of saving our ship captains from some unjustifiable custom-house interferences
                    to which they are now subjected.</p>
                <p>You will see that the method of distinguishing crude from rectified petroleum has
                    been defined anew, which seems an acknowledgment on the part of the Spanish
                    Government that I was right, if not in my interpretation of the note as it
                    formerly stood, at least in thinking it obscure.</p>
                <p>You will observe the resolute pressure which the Spanish Government brings to
                    bear on nations without special treaties.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d472-a1.xml" xpointer="d472-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
